@startuml Sequence_CursorPagination
title Cursor Pagination Flow — Product List & Sale History ([Unreleased])

actor Merchant
participant "ProductPage / HistoryPage" as UI
participant "GetProductsPage\n/ GetSalesPage" as UC
participant "ProductRepository\n/ SaleRepository" as Repo
participant "ProductLocalDatasource\n/ SaleQueryLocalDatasource" as DS
database "SQLite\n(idx_*_created_at_id_cursor)" as DB

== First Page ==
Merchant -> UI: Scroll to list
UI -> UC: call(cursor: null, pageSize: 50)
UC -> Repo: getProductsPage(cursor: null, pageSize: 50)
Repo -> DS: getProductsPage(cursor: null, pageSize: 50)

DS -> DB: SELECT * FROM products\nWHERE deleted_at IS NULL\n  [AND active = 1]\nORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC\nLIMIT 51  -- +1 to detect hasMore
DB --> DS: 51 rows (if ≥ 51, hasMore = true)
alt rows.length > pageSize
    DS -> DS: hasMore = true\nnextCursor = Cursor(rows[49].createdAt, rows[49].id)\npageRows = rows[0..49]
else rows.length ≤ pageSize
    DS -> DS: hasMore = false\nnextCursor = null\npageRows = all rows
end

DS -> DB: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM products\nWHERE deleted_at IS NULL
DB --> DS: totalCount

DS --> Repo: ProductPage(products, nextCursor, totalCount)
Repo --> UC: ProductPage
UC --> UI: ProductPage
UI --> Merchant: Render 50 items + "Showing 1-50 of {totalCount}"

== Next Page (cursor provided) ==
Merchant -> UI: Scroll to bottom (load more)
UI -> UC: call(cursor: prevNextCursor, pageSize: 50)
UC -> Repo: getProductsPage(cursor: prevNextCursor, pageSize: 50)
Repo -> DS: getProductsPage(cursor: prevNextCursor, pageSize: 50)

DS -> DB: SELECT * FROM products\nWHERE deleted_at IS NULL\n  AND (created_at, id) < (cursor.createdAt, cursor.id)\nORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC\nLIMIT 51
DB --> DS: next 51 rows
DS -> DS: same hasMore / nextCursor logic
DS --> Repo: ProductPage
Repo --> UC: ProductPage
UC --> UI: ProductPage
UI --> Merchant: Append 50 items + update "Showing 51-100 of {totalCount}"

note over DS, DB
  **Sale history** uses the same pattern via
  SaleQueryLocalDatasource.querySalesPage(),
  with optional from/to date range applied
  before the cursor predicate. Items and
  payments are hydrated only for the current
  page (batched, not N+1).
end note

@enduml
